\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces The occupancy term, refitted (heavy $T=200$, degree-$d$ responses fitted directly in coefficient space; identical machinery on every system). (a) False rate at matched efficiency $0.985$, three-event means: the fitted response on the occupancy system at $\alpha =0.05$ beats both the classical solver and the fitted response on the base system. (b) Per event: the event that is held at the efficiency ceiling on the base system (event 1) escapes it on the occupancy system: the co-hit coupling breaks the fragment/false-pair twin degeneracy.\relax }}{31}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:occfit}{{16}{31}{The occupancy term, refitted (heavy $T=200$, degree-$d$ responses fitted directly in coefficient space; identical machinery on every system). (a) False rate at matched efficiency $0.985$, three-event means: the fitted response on the occupancy system at $\alpha =0.05$ beats both the classical solver and the fitted response on the base system. (b) Per event: the event that is held at the efficiency ceiling on the base system (event 1) escapes it on the occupancy system: the co-hit coupling breaks the fragment/false-pair twin degeneracy.\relax }{figure.caption.18}{}}
