\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Logical resources of the three filters on the shared events, in the common currency of controlled-$e^{\pm iAt}$ calls (all three use the same synthesised evolution circuit; one call costs $6.2\times 10^{5}$ CX at $T=400$ globally, $\approx 900$ CX on the largest 16-segment cluster). The scaling column gives the $T$-dependence of each row; anchors are quoted at the stated $T$. The HHL column is a structure-level estimate at $n_c=6$--$8$ clock bits; the 1BQF and comb columns are measured. In the per-cluster route only the \emph  {number} of cluster instances grows with $T$ (linearly); every per-instance resource is set by the cluster size, which the no-giant-component measurement caps at $\approx 17$ segments. One-qubit gate counts track the CX counts at the same order and are omitted.\relax }}{38}{table.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
